---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { LINKS, SITE } from '../data/site';

const ga = Boolean(SITE.gaId);
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={
    ga
      ? 'How the NeuroGIDAS website handles your information. Short answer: we count visits with Google Analytics and nothing else.'
      : "How the NeuroGIDAS website handles your information. Short answer: we don't collect any through the site."
  }
  updated={ga ? 'October 21, 2026' : 'October 20, 2026'}
  summary={[
    ...(ga
      ? [
          'This website never asks for your name, email, or any other personal information.',
          'We use Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages people read. No ads, and we never sell the data.',
          'If your browser sends Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track, analytics does not load at all.',
        ]
      : [
          'This website does not ask for, collect, or store any personal information.',
          'There are no forms, accounts, ads, trackers, or analytics on this site.',
        ]),
    'Our web host keeps basic server logs to run and protect the site.',
    'If you email us, we only use your email to reply to you.',
    'Links to GroupMe, Instagram, and other sites follow those sites’ own privacy policies.',
  ]}
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    NeuroGIDAS is a student-run neuroscience and genetics club at Eastview High School in Apple Valley, Minnesota (District 196).
    This policy covers the website at neurogidas.vercel.app. When this page says “we” or “us,” it means the club. You can
    reach us at <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.email}`}>{LINKS.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect through this website</h2>
  {
    ga ? (
      <>
        <p>
          The site has no sign-up forms, no accounts, no comment boxes, and no newsletter. You can read every page without
          telling us who you are. The only thing we measure is how the site gets used, with Google Analytics.
        </p>

        <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          When you visit, Google Analytics records things like which pages you open, how long you stay, what kind of device and
          browser you use, your rough location (city or region), and the site that sent you here. It does not store your IP
          address, and it never gets your name or email.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use this only to see totals, like how many people visited after an Instagram post or which meetings people read
          about most. We turned off Google’s advertising and Google signals features, so the data is not used for ads or linked
          to your Google account. Google keeps the detailed data for a limited time (14 months at most) and then deletes it.
          You can read how Google handles it in{' '}
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">
            How Google uses information from sites that use its services
          </a>
          .
        </p>
        <p>
          You can turn it off by turning on Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track in your browser, by blocking cookies, or
          with Google’s <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">opt-out add-on</a>. Our{' '}
          <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> has the details.
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <p>
        Nothing. The site has no sign-up forms, no accounts, no comment boxes, and no newsletter. We don’t use analytics tools,
        advertising, tracking pixels, or social media widgets. You can read every page without telling us who you are.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <h2>Information our web host handles</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted by <a href="https://vercel.com" rel="noopener">Vercel</a>. Like almost every web host, Vercel’s servers
    automatically record basic technical details when a page is requested, such as your IP address, your browser type, the page
    you asked for, and the time. Vercel uses this to deliver the site and protect it from attacks. We don’t use these logs to
    figure out who you are. You can read how Vercel handles this data in the{' '}
    <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">Vercel Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our fonts and images are stored on the same host, so your browser doesn’t contact any other company to load them
    {ga ? ' (Google Analytics is the one exception, described above).' : '.'}
  </p>

  <h2>If you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we get your email address and whatever you write. We only use it to answer you and to keep you updated
    about the club if you ask us to. We don’t sell it, trade it, or give it to anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to other services, including GroupMe, Instagram, Google Calendar, Gmail, miRcore, our co-president’s
    textbook, and free research databases like NCBI. When you click a link, you leave our site and that service’s own privacy
    policy applies. For example, joining our GroupMe is covered by GroupMe’s privacy policy, not this one. We don’t control
    those sites.
  </p>

  <h2>Students and children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is meant for high school students, families, and teachers. We don’t collect names, emails, or other personal
    information through the site, so we don’t knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13.
    {ga && 'Google Analytics only gives us visit totals that don’t say who anyone is.'} If you think a child has sent us
    personal information by email, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Photos and names on this site</h2>
  <p>
    The names and photos of club officers appear on the Team page with their permission. If you are pictured or named on this
    site and want something changed or taken down, email us and we will do it as soon as we can.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what information we have about you (usually just emails you sent us) and ask us to delete it. Email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.email}`}>{LINKS.email}</a> and we will respond within a reasonable time.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The whole site is served over a secure connection (HTTPS). Since we don’t collect personal information through the site,
    there is no personal data stored here to be exposed.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we ever change how the site works, for example by adding a sign-up form{ga ? '' : ' or analytics'}, we will update this
    page first and change the date at the top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy? Email <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.email}`}>{LINKS.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
